[SIZE="4"][B]RPQuest[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE="4"][COLOR="DarkRed"][B]Notice:[/B][/COLOR] I'm actively developing this. Being a social-focused addon there are many aspects that I need to test with others. If you are willing to help test it or have comments, contact me![/SIZE]

A native, [B]zero-dependency[/B] add-on for [B]The Elder Scrolls Online[/B] that lets you create, play, complete, and share [B]custom Roleplay quests[/B] directly inside ESO's native UI.

[SIZE="3"][B]Key Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Native Quest Journal Integration (J):[/B] Adds a dedicated [B]RPQuests[/B] tab inside the standard Quest Journal with exclusive accordion sections for [B]Pending[/B], [B]Quests[/B], [B]Completed[/B], [B]Preparing[/B], and [B]Sent[/B] (keeping an active section expanded whenever quests exist and remembering the last open section and selected quest across sessions), plus native Journal keybind shortcuts for [B]Show on Map[/B] and [B]Abandon[/B].
[*][B]Reticle NPC Target Capture:[/B] Aim at any living NPC and press your keybind to register objectives automatically. Capturing the same NPC name multiple times stacks into [I]Imp x3[/I]; different named NPCs are managed individually from the editor's target dropdown (with delete selected and delete all buttons), per-target [B]Map Search Area Size[/B] ([I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I]), an [B]Optional target[/B] checkbox, per-target [B]Location[/B] conditions ([B]Required[/B] within [I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I] ([I]8m[/I] / [I]23m[/I] / [I]39m[/I] / [I]54m[/I] / [I]70m[/I]) or optional—eliminating a [B]Required[/B] target outside the radius marks the quest as [I]Failed[/I]), and two optional elimination message fields ([I]On elimination[/I] and [I]On elimination (location met)[/I]).
[*][B]Hidden Discovery Points:[/B] Stand at an exploration spot and click the [B]+[/B] icon button ([B]Add point[/B]) in the editor's [B]Hidden Discovery Points (Optional)[/B] accordion with a configurable trigger radius dropdown ([I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I] — [I]8m[/I], [I]23m[/I], [I]39m[/I], [I]54m[/I], [I]70m[/I]), a [B]Required[/B] checkbox per point (tagged [I][Req][/I] in the point dropdown), up/down arrow buttons to reorder points, a [B]Sequential order (unlock points one by one)[/B] checkbox (evaluating and showing player map pins one point at a time in order while creators keep seeing all points), and a required [B]Discovery Point Message[/B]. Creators automatically see purple discovery areas on the map (with discovery index and message summary tooltips), while players keep them hidden by default with an optional spoiler-free [B]Discovery[/B] checkbox in [B]MAP MARKERS[/B].
[*][B]Stealth / Undetected Condition (Disabled / Optional / Required) & Completion Message:[/B] Choose via dropdown whether staying undetected (no Justice bounty, infamy, or failed pickpocket in the quest area) is [B]Disabled[/B], [B]Optional[/B] (records detection without failing), or [B]Required[/B] (immediately fails the quest if detected), and optionally set a custom [B]Completion Message[/B] displayed when the quest finishes.
[*][B]Quest Icons:[/B] Optionally assign a native icon ([B]Black Hand[/B], [B]Search[/B], or [B]Steal[/B]) in the quest editor to visually identify quest themes in the journal list, quest details, and shared quests.
[*][B]World Map Search, Location & Discovery Areas (M):[/B] Supports per-target emerald-green search circles on the World Map with a brief initial pulse, deterministic fixed random offset, and automatic radius scaling on city/subzone maps, optional soft-orange captured target location circles (both layers clear per target as each objective is completed), and purple discovery point circles (automatically shown for creators in Edit/Preparing/Sent and hidden by default for players, clearing each point as it is discovered). In the editor's [B]Mission Settings[/B] accordion, [B]Recommend no map markers to player[/B] (enabled by default on new drafts) displays [B]Show map markers: not recommended[/B] inside [B]MISSION DETAILS[/B]; for players, the [B]MAP MARKERS[/B] section shows applicable [B]Search Areas[/B], [B]Location[/B], and [B]Discovery[/B] checkboxes (all off by default) that can be toggled independently per quest (while [B]Show on Map[/B] remains available whenever a map/area is defined). When zoomed out to a parent zone or Tamriel world map, displays a medium pulsing emerald reference area with a deterministic offset (keeping the objective inside without revealing its exact spot), and automatically hides it when zooming back into the target map or upon completion/deactivation.
[*][B]Native NPC Dialogue Injection & Objectives:[/B] Open dialogue ([B]E[/B]) with up to 4 native ESO NPCs and click [B]+ Last NPC[/B] in the editor to bind custom RPQuest dialogue lines, per-NPC player response options, and an optional [B]Required[/B] toggle per NPC, injected seamlessly into the native interaction window without altering original NPC options. Dialogue execution is persisted in SavedVariables across reloads, displays live dialogue progress in [B]TASKS[/B], and automatically completes dialogue-only quests (with 0 targets and 0 discovery points) once all configured dialogues are spoken.
[*][B]Combat & Discovery Tracking + Native Alerts:[/B] Tracks kills and exploration proximity, triggering native Center Screen Announcements and official quest sounds.
[*][B]Local Quest Master Testing & Reset:[/B] Use [B]Test Quest[/B] / [B]Stop Testing[/B] on any [B]Preparing[/B] or [B]Sent[/B] quest to test the full flow locally before sending, [B]Reset[/B] to restart a prepared or [I]Failed[/I] quest, or [B]Migrate[/B] if an older draft needs schema updating.
[*][B]1-to-1 In-Game Mail Flow (No Copy/Paste):[/B] Assign a single [I]@AccountName[/I] recipient (and optional [I]To (Character)[/I] / [I]From (Character)[/I] account-character selector) in the quest editor and click [B]Send Quest[/B] from the quest detail pane—sending directly when [I]@AccountName[/I] is already set, or opening the Mail Send pane with an optional roleplay message and live 1–6 part counter when no recipient is set (ESO prevents sending mail to your own account). Incoming quest mails are automatically ingested into the player's [B]Pending[/B] list with an alert and [B]Accept[/B] / [B]Reject[/B] buttons (mismatched-language quest mails are automatically rejected with an error alert). Accepting, completing, failing, or rejecting a quest automatically mails the result back to the Quest Master, updating the contract's resolution ([I]Accepted[/I] / [I]Completed[/I] / [I]Failed[/I] / [I]Rejected[/I]) separately from its lifecycle ([I]Draft[/I] / [I]Sent[/I] / [I]Received[/I]).
[*][B]Account-Wide Persistence & Auto-Localization:[/B] Stores quests, progress, and last open Journal section / selected quest account-wide via SavedVariables (matching ESO's account-wide mail, with automatic migration from legacy per-character data) and auto-detects all 7 official ESO client languages (English, German, Spanish, French, Japanese, Russian, Simplified Chinese).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Keybinds (Settings -> Controls -> RPQuest - Custom Quests)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Capture Target Under Reticle (NPC):[/B] Captures the living NPC currently under your reticle into the quest draft.
[*][B]Open / Close Custom Quests Tab:[/B] Opens or closes the Quest Journal directly on the [B]RPQuests[/B] tab.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Quick Start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Create a Quest:[/B] Open the Quest Journal ([B]J[/B]), switch to the [B]RPQuests[/B] tab, and click [B]+ New[/B] (which immediately creates a [B]New Quest[/B] draft in [B]Preparing[/B] and opens it in the editor). Use the single-open animated accordion sections to set Title, [B]Description / Story[/B], [B]Quest Icon[/B] ([I]None[/I], [I]Black Hand[/I], [I]Search[/I], or [I]Steal[/I]), per-target [B]Map Search Area Size[/B], [B]Optional target[/B], [B]Location[/B], and optional [B]On elimination[/B] / [B]On elimination (location met)[/B] messages, plus [B]Completion Message[/B], [B]Undetected Stealth Condition[/B] ([I]Disabled[/I], [I]Optional[/I], or [I]Required[/I]), and [B]Recommend no map markers to player[/B] in [B]Mission Settings[/B], as well as optional [B]NPC Dialogues[/B]. Aim at NPCs and press your capture keybind, or stand at discovery spots and click the [B]+[/B] icon button ([B]Add point[/B]) in [B]Hidden Discovery Points (Optional)[/B] (each discovery point requires a [B]Discovery Point Message[/B]). In-progress edits are automatically preserved when switching quests or closing the journal, or click [B]Save Draft[/B] to save and finish editing (free-form and dialogue-only quests without NPC targets or discovery points can also be tested and sent; use [B]Abandon[/B] in the bottom keybind strip to delete a draft).
[*][B]Send to a Player:[/B] Set the recipient [I]@AccountName[/I] (and optional character name) in the quest editor, select the saved quest in [B]Preparing[/B], and click [B]Send Quest[/B] in the quest detail pane. The player receives an alert and can [B]Accept[/B] or [B]Reject[/B] the quest directly from [B]Pending[/B] in their [B]RPQuests[/B] tab. Note: quests require the same game client language as the creator so NPC objectives and dialogues match.
[*][B]Play & Auto-Report:[/B] Accepting the quest activates tracking and injected NPC dialogues immediately; map markers are off by default and can be toggled independently per quest in [B]MAP MARKERS[/B] ([B]Search Areas[/B] / [B]Location[/B] / [B]Discovery[/B]). Accepting, completing, or rejecting the quest automatically mails the result back to the Quest Master.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]How to Use / Guide[/B][/SIZE]

[B]1. Roles: Quest Master vs. Player[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Quest Master (Creator):[/B] Authors custom quests in [B]Preparing[/B], captures NPC targets or discovery spots in the world, tests locally with [B]Test Quest[/B], configures optional rules or dialogues, and dispatches contracts to a player via in-game mail. Once sent, the Quest Master tracks live progress and final outcomes in [B]Sent[/B].
[*][B]Player (Recipient):[/B] Receives quest offers in [B]Pending[/B], reviews the briefing, and chooses [B]Accept[/B] or [B]Reject[/B]. Active quests are tracked automatically in-world, and results are mailed back to the Quest Master with zero manual copy/paste.
[/LIST]

[B]2. Journal Sections (Exclusive Accordion)[/B]
The [B]RPQuests[/B] tab inside your Quest Journal ([B]J[/B]) uses an exclusive accordion—expanding one section collapses the others so your list stays tidy (one active section stays expanded whenever quests exist, and your last open section and selected quest are restored across sessions):
[LIST]
[*][B]Pending:[/B] Incoming quest offers waiting for you to [B]Accept[/B] or [B]Reject[/B].
[*][B]Quests:[/B] Your currently accepted and active quests (including [I]Failed[/I] quests that can be restarted with [B]Reset[/B]). Select a quest to view [B]MISSION DETAILS[/B] and [B]TASKS[/B], toggle applicable [B]MAP MARKERS[/B] ([B]Search Areas[/B] / [B]Location[/B] / [B]Discovery[/B]), toggle tracking, jump to the map ([B]Show on Map[/B]), [B]Abandon[/B], or manually complete it via [B]Complete[/B] (for pure [I]free-form[/I] quests with no targets/discoveries/dialogues, or once all mandatory targets are done; missing any [B]Required[/B] discovery or dialogue at resolution fails the quest).
[*][B]Completed:[/B] Archive of finished quests you have played, including final stealth and optional objective outcomes.
[*][B]Preparing:[/B] Unsent quest drafts you are creating or editing as a Quest Master. You can also copy any [B]Preparing[/B] or [B]Sent[/B] quest into [B]Preparing[/B] to create a fresh editable draft, test it locally ([B]Test Quest[/B]), or migrate legacy schemas ([B]Migrate[/B]).
[*][B]Sent:[/B] Contracts you have already mailed to players, showing [I]From:[/I] / [I]To:[/I] names, lifecycle and live resolution ([I]Sent[/I], [I]Accepted[/I], [I]Rejected[/I], [I]Completed[/I], [I]Failed[/I]), and automatic completion/failure results (such as [I]Undetected[/I] vs [I]Detected[/I] and optional objectives).
[/LIST]

[B]3. Quest Building Blocks[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Targets (NPC Elimination & Player Duels):[/B] Aim at any living NPC or another player and press your [B]Capture Target Under Reticle (NPC)[/B] keybind. Player targets are tracked as duel objectives ([I]EVENT_DUEL_FINISHED[/I], counting local victories and opponent forfeits while ignoring defeats). Capturing the same target name multiple times stacks into a count (e.g. [I]Imp x3[/I]); different targets become separate objectives managed from the target dropdown (with delete selected and delete all buttons). For each target, you can set [B]Map Search Area Size[/B] ([I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I]), toggle [B]Optional target[/B] (allowing the player to finish the quest once all mandatory objectives are complete), configure [B]Location[/B] ([B]Capture Loc[/B], [I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I] ([I]8m[/I] / [I]23m[/I] / [I]39m[/I] / [I]54m[/I] / [I]70m[/I]) radius, and the [B]Required[/B] checkbox—unchecked means optional/anywhere, checked fails the quest if eliminated outside the radius), and enter optional [I]On elimination[/I] and [I]On elimination (location met)[/I] messages.
[*][B]Hidden Discovery Points:[/B] Stand at an exploration spot and click the [B]+[/B] icon button ([B]Add point[/B]) in the [B]Hidden Discovery Points (Optional)[/B] accordion. You can configure the trigger radius ([I]Tiny[/I] / [I]Small[/I] / [I]Medium[/I] / [I]Large[/I] / [I]Huge[/I] — [I]8m[/I], [I]23m[/I], [I]39m[/I], [I]54m[/I], or [I]70m[/I]), mark individual points as [B]Required[/B] ([I][Req][/I]), reorder them with the up/down arrow buttons, enable [B]Sequential order (unlock points one by one)[/B] so each point only unlocks after the previous one is discovered, and must write a [B]Discovery Point Message[/B] before saving, testing, or sending. Discovery points remain hidden on the map and compass by default for players to avoid spoilers (creators see purple discovery areas automatically, and players can toggle [B]Discovery[/B] in [B]MAP MARKERS[/B]).
[*][B]Stealth (Undetected) & Completion Message:[/B] Use the [B]Undetected Stealth Condition[/B] dropdown in the quest editor ([I]Disabled[/I], [I]Optional[/I], or [I]Required[/I]) to track stealth as a bonus condition or fail the quest immediately upon detection. You can also enter an optional [B]Completion Message[/B] shown upon finishing.
[*][B]World Map Search, Location & Discovery Areas (M):[/B] Displays per-target approximate search circles using a fixed random offset (with automatic radius scaling on city/subzone maps) and optional soft-orange captured target location circles; circles clear per target as each objective is completed (as well as when the quest is completed or deactivated). All three map layers (Search Areas, Location, and Discovery) are off by default for players and can be toggled independently per quest in [B]MAP MARKERS[/B] (while any [B]Show map markers: not recommended[/B] note from [B]Recommend no map markers to player[/B] appears in [B]MISSION DETAILS[/B]); [B]Show on Map[/B] ([B]M[/B]) remains available whenever a map/area is defined.
[*][B]NPC Dialogues:[/B] Open dialogue ([B]E[/B]) with up to 4 native ESO NPCs and click [B]+ Last NPC[/B] to capture them into the quest's [B]NPC Dialogues[/B] section, mark any dialogue as [B]Required[/B] ([I][Req][/I]), and write a custom player response option and NPC reply for each. When the player speaks to those NPCs, your custom line is injected seamlessly into the native dialogue window without modifying original game options, dialogue progress is saved across reloads and shown in [B]TASKS[/B], and dialogue-only quests auto-complete once all dialogues are executed.
[/LIST]

[B]4. In-Game Mail Flow (Automatic)[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Sending:[/B] Enter the recipient's [I]@AccountName[/I] (and optional [I]To (Character)[/I] name) in the quest editor, save the quest, and click [B]Send Quest[/B] in the quest detail pane. When [I]@AccountName[/I] is already set in the editor, clicking [B]Send Quest[/B] sends directly; if no recipient is set, the Mail Send pane opens with an [I]Optional Roleplay Message[/I] field and a live part counter (1–6 parts). Both players must be on the same megaserver (e.g. PC-NA or PC-EU) and use the same client language, and ESO blocks sending mail to your own account.
[*][B]Arrival Announcement & Optional Auto-Open:[/B] When a quest mail arrives, RPQuest ingests it automatically and displays an on-screen announcement alerting the player that a new quest is waiting in [B]Pending[/B] (or rejects and alerts if the quest language does not match the client). You can optionally enable [B]Auto-open RPQuests journal when receiving a new quest[/B] at the bottom of the quest list panel to automatically open the [B]RPQuests[/B] tab and select the new quest (skipped while in combat).
[*][B]Accepting & Rejecting:[/B] Clicking [B]Accept[/B] activates the quest and NPC dialogues (map markers remain off by default until toggled in the quest details), and notifies the Quest Master. Clicking [B]Reject[/B] declines the offer and notifies the Quest Master.
[*][B]Completion & Failure Reporting:[/B] When the player finishes all objectives (or manually completes a [I]free-form[/I] quest or one with only optional targets remaining), or fails a required condition (such as stealth, target location, or a [B]Required[/B] discovery/dialogue missed at resolution), RPQuest automatically mails the report back to the Quest Master and updates the contract's resolution in [B]Sent[/B].
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]External Libraries:[/B] None (Zero-Dependency)
[*][B]Languages:[/B] English (en), German (de), Spanish (es), French (fr), Japanese (jp), Russian (ru), Simplified Chinese (zh)
[/LIST]

